Pumpkin Chocolate Harvest Cake
  --Nordic Ware

2/3 c softened butter or shortening
2 c sugar
1 egg
2 egg whites
2 1/2 c flour
1/2 tsp baking powder
1 1/2 tsp baking soda
1 tsp salt
1 1/4 tsp cinnamon
1/4 tsp nutmeg
15 oz can solid-pack pumpkin
1/2 c water
3 tbsp cocoa
1 tbsp water

Heat oven to 350F (175C). Grease and flour a Bundt pan; set aside. In large bowl, beat butter and sugar until creamy. Add egg and egg whites; mix until well blended. Add flour, baking powder, baking soda, salt, cinnamon, nutmeg, pumpkin and 1/2 c water; mix on low speed until blended, scraping bowl often. Increase speed to medium and beat 2 min. Remove 3/4 c of the batter and put in a small bowl. Spoon remaining batter into prepared pan. To reserved batter, add cocoa and 1 tbsp water; stir to combine. Place spoonfuls of chocolate batter on top of batter in pan. Using a knife, swirl chocolate batter into pumpkin batter to marble. Bake 40-47 min, until toothpick inserted comes out clean. Cool 10 min in pan; remove from pan and cool complete.
